  "kind": "recipe",
  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "standard",
    "description": "eugr's (Eugene Rakhmatulin) spark-vllm-docker deepseek-v4-flash recipe for DeepSeek's DeepSeek-V4-Flash (MIT; checkpoint revision 60d8d707) served by vLLM on two Sparks. Runs eugr's published vllm-node image (nightly-20260929, digest pinned; its build-metadata records spark-vllm-docker 42f62e34, vLLM 0.30.1rc1.dev336+gaf5b4857e and FlashInfer 4a638133) with upstream's launch: InstantTensor loading, FP8 KV cache with block size 256, MTP speculative decoding with two tokens, deepseek_v4 tokenizer, tool-call and reasoning parsers with thinking on and high reasoning effort by default, 500,000-token context (VLLM_ALLOW_LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN), four sequences, 8,192 batched tokens and memory utilisation 0.8 (upstream defaults), with DG_JIT_USE_NVRTC=0 and VLLM_USE_BREAKABLE_CUDAGRAPH=1. Tensor parallel 2 across the pair uses vLLM's native multi-node launch, eugr's default no-Ray cluster mode, so upstream's --distributed-executor-backend ray is dropped. Upstream's `--default-chat-template-kwargs.thinking=true` and `.reasoning_effort=high` are passed as one JSON `--default-chat-template-kwargs` value (equivalent). The recipe is cluster-only upstream (the checkpoint does not fit one Spark). No upstream performance claims are recorded. Upstream repository MIT. Physical Spark acceptance is pending.",
    "tags": [
      "candidate",
      "deepseek",
      "deepseek-v4",
      "dual",
      "eugr",
      "executable",
      "mtp",
      "reasoning",
      "spark",
      "tool-use",
      "vllm"
    ],
    "title": "DeepSeek V4 Flash MTP vLLM two Sparks (eugr)"
  },
